# llm_alt_s_after_atty_init_bash — regression pin: after the user
# runs `eval "$(atty init bash)"`, the very next `#: …` + Alt+S
# should fire the dialog (NOT print the "needs OSC 133" gate
# error). The init snippet wraps PS1 with `;A` / `;B` markers and
# adds `__atty_osc133_d` to PROMPT_COMMAND, so by the time the
# user types the next character at the prompt the LLM module's
# osc133_capture.active should already be true.
#
# Without this scenario the integration path is untested — every
# other dialog scenario sets PS1 manually with the markers
# inlined, which bypasses the `atty init bash` → PROMPT_COMMAND →
# PS1 expansion chain that real users hit.
#
# We send Alt+S via the kitty kbd CSI-u byte form (`\x1b[115;3u`)
# because atty pushes the disambiguate flag at startup — real
# Ghostty / kitty / foot sessions will only emit this form, not
# the legacy `\x1bs` (which the e2e harness historically used but
# does not exercise the real-terminal code path).

cols 120
rows 10
timeout_ms 8000

spawn $ATTY bash --norc --noprofile -i
wait_for "$"

# Run the real `atty init bash` snippet inline. Once eval
# returns, PROMPT_COMMAND fires `__atty_osc133_d` (emits `;D;0`)
# and `__atty_osc133_wrap_ps1` (wraps PS1 with `;A` / `;B`).
# The next prompt redraw emits the wrapped markers — that's
# what flips osc133_capture.active inside the LLM runtime.
#
# `$ATTY_BIN` is exposed by the harness — the forced PATH
# doesn't include the `.zig-cache/o/<hash>/` bin dir.
type "eval \"$($ATTY_BIN init bash)\"\r"
wait_for "$"
sleep 300

# Enter AI mode.
type "#: print ok"
sleep 300

# Alt+S via the kitty kbd CSI-u encoding (115 = 's', mod 3 = Alt).
# This is what Ghostty / kitty / foot send under atty's default
# `\x1b[>1u` push. The dual binding in defaults.zig is what
# closes the gap with the legacy `\x1bs` form.
type "\x1b[115;3u"
sleep 500

# If the OSC 133 gate is closed (regression), the bar prints the
# ⚠ "needs OSC 133" hint. If the fix is in place, the fixture
# response lands on the prompt as the suggested command and the
# state moves to .suggesting (hint above the bar is the
# description, not the gate-failure message).
snapshot dialog_started

# Cleanly cancel + exit so exit_code matches the golden. Esc
# under kitty kbd is `\x1b[27u`.
type "\x1b[27u"
sleep 100
type "\x15"
sleep 100
type "exit\r"
exit_code 0
